-## General Advice
-
-- send small code chunks ideally as when code is too long it seems to confuse ChatGPT.
-- splitting a big problem in smaller chunks helps a big lot, regardless how small the steps are but anyways etc.
-- if you send image files to it so it analyzes it them, and your screen resolution is higher than say 1920 x 1080 (e.g. a 4K screen even if your resolution is say 1920 x 1080, the screenshots would be on your screen's resolution if game is fullscreen or windowed maximized if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc), consider reducing your game resolution to 1920 x 1080 (or in windowed mode you can keep a higher resolution but click on the square window button on top right to minimize the game window if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc) as it seems that chatgpt 5.1 (for example but anyways etc) can analyze them faster from a prompt, and i asked it as well and it says so as well, but check if accurate and/or updated but anyways etc.
-- chatgpt is very good at doing charts comparisons, unit tests (using stub or real (for example xml or pasted in chat box, etc)), but check to be sure if works well (for/+/-in) you(r) case
-- it (chatgpt) can also create scripts to generate such charts so you don't even have to bother dealing with limits and such, for example the [flatten_leaders_data_to_csv.py script](README_Python_Scripts.md#flatten_leaders_data_to_csvpy) (or similar format maybe alternatively if you want) format
